        "### Homework Hack: JSON Character Sheet & Dot Notation\n",
        "\n",
        "Create a character sheet using a JavaScript object containing `name`, `username`, a nested `character_info` object (`level`, `class`, `health`), and `skills` array.\n",
        "\n",
        "Then:\n",
        "1. Access and display the properties using **chained dot notation**.\n",
        "2. Convert the object into a JSON string using `JSON.stringify()`.\n",
        "3. Print the JSON string and attempt dot notation directly on the string.\n",
        "4. Parse the JSON string back into an object using `JSON.parse()`.\n",
        "5. Print the parsed object and access properties using dot notation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "b83e16f4",
      "metadata": {
        "vscode": {
          "languageId": "javascript"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "%%js\n",
        "// CODE_RUNNER: Homework - Create a character sheet, convert to JSON, and test dot notation.\n",
        "const character_sheet = {\n",
        "    name: \"Eldrin\",\n",
        "    username: \"ShadowBlade99\",\n",
        "    character_info: {\n",
        "        level: 85,\n",
        "        class: \"Rogue\",\n",
        "        health: 540\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    skills: [\"Stealth\", \"Backstab\", \"Poison Dart\", \"Shadow Step\"]\n",
        "};\n",
        "\n",
        "// 1. Access properties via dot notation\n",
        "console.log(\"Name:\", character_sheet.name);\n",
        "console.log(\"Username:\", character_sheet.username);\n",
        "console.log(\"Level (Chained Dot Notation):\", character_sheet.character_info.level);\n",
        "\n",
        "// 2. Convert to JSON string\n",
        "const jsonString = JSON.stringify(character_sheet);\n",
        "console.log(\"--- JSON String Output ---\");\n",
        "console.log(jsonString);\n",
        "console.log(\"Dot notation directly on JSON string:\", jsonString.name); // Returns undefined\n",
        "\n",
        "// 3. Parse back into JS Object\n",
        "const parsedCharacterSheet = JSON.parse(jsonString);\n",
        "console.log(\"--- Parsed JavaScript Object Output ---\");\n",
        "console.log(\"Parsed Name (Dot Notation):\", parsedCharacterSheet.name);\n",
        "console.log(\"Parsed Level (Chained Dot Notation):\", parsedCharacterSheet.character_info.level);"
      ]
    },
